.TH "Docv::Viewer::Frame" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Viewer::Frame \- The screen layout: a title row with the name, the page\(aqs heading centered and a close mark, a line under it, the content with one blank column of padding on either side, and the vertical scrollbar in the last column (only its thumb is drawn).
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBstruct Docv::Viewer::Frame\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
The screen layout: a title row with the name, the page\(aqs heading
centered and a close mark, a line under it, the
content with one blank column of padding on either side, and the
vertical scrollbar in the last column (only its thumb is drawn). Below
the content the horizontal scrollbar runs as a line (thumb \fB\%\[u2501]\fR, track
\fB\%\[u2500]\fR), then the status row. A thumb that fills its track means
everything fits. A regular dock (\fB\%Dock\fR) takes the first \fIdock\fR
columns of the content rows; the content area starts after it.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
